dustries, as well as the public sector. the company has a collaboration with OpenAI, L.L.C. for the development of AI solutions for joint enterprise customers that deliver tangible return on investment. The company was formerly known as Snowflake Computing, Inc. and changed its name to Snowflake Inc. in April 2019. Snowflake Inc. was incorporated in 2012 and is based in Menlo Park, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sridhar  Ramaswamy Ph.D. | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $499K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 51%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $119K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $170K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Snowflake Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $97.3B market cap on $4.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +31% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +12.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -63% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 66% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -28.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -173.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.9%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 34% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 640% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":6.396351494713133},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 38% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $289.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 697% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Snowflake (SNOW) Fully Valued After Its Latest AI Upgrades?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nyse-snow/snowflake/news/is-snowflake-snow-fully-valued-after-its-latest-ai-upgrades","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793940976.246,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.831,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Why Did Snowflake (NYSE:SNOW) Shares Slide Amid AI Spending Fears?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/technical-analysis/why-did-snowflake-nysesnow-shares-slide-amid-ai-spending-fears","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793906760.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.241,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Palantir Grew Revenue 96% and the Stock Still Fell. Here\u2019s Where the Price Target Goes","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/palantir-grew-revenue-96-stock-160308000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793981371.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","analyst_action"]},{"title":"3 AI Infrastructure Stocks to Watch After the Data Centre Selloff","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/kr/tech/kose-a005930/samsung-electronics-shares/news/3-ai-infrastructure-stocks-to-watch-after-the-data-centre-se","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793979079.969,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.66,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Rep. Maria Elvira Salazar Has Bought Up to $60K Worth Of NVIDIA Stock: Here\u2019s What You Should Know","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/government/26/11/62982002/rep-maria-elvira-salazar-has-bought-60k-worth-nvidia-stock-here-s-what-you-should-know","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793977211.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Palantir Shed Nearly 20% Over 12 Months: This Wall Street Desk Predicts 76% Gains Moving Forward","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/palantir-shed-nea